\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Light of those whose dreary dwelling 
\par Borders on the shades of death,
\par Come, and by Thy love's revealing 
\par Dissipate the clouds beneath ;
\par The new heaven and earth's Creator,
\par In our deepest darkness rise,
\par Scattering all the night of nature,
\par Pouring eyesight on our eyes.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Still we wait for Thine appearing ;
\par Life and joy Thy beams impart,
\par Chasing all our fears, and cheering 
\par Every poor benighted the heart:
\par Come, and manifest the favour
\par God hath for our ransomed race ;
\par Come, Thou universal Saviour,
\par Come, and bring the gospel grace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Save us in Thy great compassion,
\par O Thou mild, pacific Prince ;
\par Give the knowledge of salvation,
\par Give the pardon of our sins :
\par By Thy all-restoring merit
\par Every burdened soul release ;
\par Every weary, wandering spirit
\par Guide into Thy perfect peace. \tab 
\par                                    Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

